<title>MEXICO: Mexico approves 25 pct wage hike for IMSS workers.</title>
<headline>Mexico approves 25 pct wage hike for IMSS workers.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-09-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexican officials have approved a 25 percent wage hike for thousands of workers of the state-run social security system, officials said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Genaro Borrego, head of the Mexican Social Security Institute (IMSS), told Mexico's Radio Red that IMSS workers would receive a 25 percent wage hike effective September 16.</p>
<p>Earlier, state-owned news agency Notimex said the IMSS had approved a 22 percent wage hike.</p>
<p>-- David Luhnow, Mexico City newsroom 525 7289565</p>
